A||||6||Posthumane||Water Pump?!?||||8||
Z||000000||Posthumane||12-27-2001||03:23 PM||||I finally had a chance to get under my 84 SE to see if I could tell where the coolant was coming from. I thought that I may have blown a head gasket because it was leaking lots of coolant, was lacking power, and the car started rolling down a very slight slope when I left it in first gear w/out the parking brake (lack of comp?). However, I looked under the car today and the coolant seems to be coming out of the bleed hole on the water pump. Problem is, I replaced the water pump just a few months ago. Also, this started rather suddenly, as opposed to gradually starting to leak (and believe me, it leaks ALOT). Could it be that I blew the head gasket in the spot right next to the water pump and it's just leaking around it? I don't see any coolant on top of the w/p but it seems to be all over the bottom of the engine. What should I do??||||reg||8
Z||000001||West Coast Fiero||12-27-2001||08:14 PM||||on the 4 cyl there is a 90 degree ( for lack of a better discriptive word ) part that locates the water pump just off of the block - check to see thatn this part is leaking where it mounts to the block, this has been very common<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000002||Posthumane||12-27-2001||10:57 PM||||Thanx. I took off that whole assembly that attaches to the block and it seems to be fine. I also checked the compressiion and it's 125 psi across all cylinders, so I guess the lack thereof must have been a one time thing. I bought a new waterpump and I'm going to install it now, and see if the problem goes away. I remember the last time my w/p went the engine started running poorly, so it may be the same again.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jncomutt||12-28-2001||01:41 AM||||Posthumane, keep me updated.  I just noticed lots of coolent on the pass. side of the cradle on my 84.  Also, When I started it 1 time, ti made a terrible tapping noise that sped up as the idle increased.  I shut the car off, started it back up and was gone.  I havn't been able to reproduce it, but I think it may be the pump..<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Posthumane||12-28-2001||02:24 AM||||Jn, if you look under the car you should see a small bleed hole on the bottom of the water pump. If there's coolant coming out of there then it's a bad w/p. Ran me about $35 cdn after core rebate. The ticking that you heard may have been the lifters. Sometimes when I start my car up it takes a second or two to get the oil pressure up to par, especially when it's cold, and with low oil pres. the hydraulic lifters are too short and you end up with valve lash. Check your oil level if it does it again. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||West Coast Fiero||12-28-2001||12:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jncomutt:<BR><B>Posthumane, keep me updated.  I just noticed lots of coolent on the pass. side of the cradle on my 84.  Also, When I started it 1 time, ti made a terrible tapping noise that sped up as the idle increased.  I shut the car off, started it back up and was gone.  I havn't been able to reproduce it, but I think it may be the pump..</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>the last 2 times I replaced a water pump on a 4 cylinder I noticed that afterwords it would not want to rotate freely on one spot out of its full 360 degrees of rotation. What happened was the massive cast impeller was striking the inner housing of the w/p. The first time we said screw it and started the car, made the same sound you were reffering to, the second replacement - I took a a file to the housing to give the impeller some clearance.<P> was the leak ever found on the 4 cylinder in question here?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000006||Posthumane||12-28-2001||06:17 PM||||Ya it was a bad water pump. I replaced it and the leak is gone. I think I may have had the belt too tight since I only had the pump on there for less than a year. I replaced the belt with a new one, because the other one looked quite old and needed to be pretty tight to not squeal. I never had a clearance problem with the water pump. Maybe your housing was different from mine.||||reg||1
